{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_014wVKPbiCTqE7rF5N95op1Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a single-folder personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty that has grown a substantial R&D control surface on top. Grounded from the project docs:\n\n- **Purpose:** A markdown-backed task/project manager (\"productivity system\") for one user, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` â€” no database, no syncing, plain-text files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, etc.) as the source of truth.\n\n- **What it ships (core):** `anchor_gui.py`, a self-contained Python-stdlib HTTP server that renders an interactive browser dashboard at `http://localhost:8777`, reading/writing the markdown directly. It runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` (auto-start). A CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) does the same operations from the command line and generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Task lifecycle:** Tasks move through Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled / Saved-for-Later / Restored, each stored in its own markdown archive, with optional Notes fields â€” all editable from the browser UI or CLI verbs (`done`, `add`, `capture`, `cancel`, `save`, `restore`).\n\n- **R&D \"cockpit\" layer (the bulk of recent work):** A per-project window that manages \"trio\"-driven R&D â€” the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill pipeline â€” as durable, isolated, server-side terminal sessions. Built across four iterations (v2 sessions/summaries/grass, v3 \"Mission Control,\" v4 \"Project Cockpit,\" all merged to master). Each lane (Research Â· Planning Â· Build Â· Deliverables Â· Grass) shows its most-recent session as a tile with one status light; clicking expands an inline panel with a cached summary plus a real resizable terminal.\n\n- **Notable engineering decisions:** Real ConPTY terminals via `pywinpty` â€” the *one* declared exception to the otherwise strict stdlib-only / no-native-deps rule (imported lazily in `pty_manager.py`, degrades gracefully if absent). Per-session git-worktree isolation, proactive cached project/session summaries, a hand-rolled stdlib WebSocket transport, a Claudeâ†”Gemini engine toggle, and a deliverable-launch-by-type system.\n\n- **Self-verification:** A daily 5:00 AM healthcheck (`anchor_healthcheck.py`, Task Scheduler) that parses every markdown file, boots a throwaway server on a test port, and walks the entire v2/v3/v4 R&D surface fully stubbed (no live `claude`, never touching `:8777` or real data), writing a dated report and surfacing failures as a red dashboard banner.\n\n- **Declared deliverable:** `anchor_gui.py` itself â€” pinned as the project's runnable deliverable, previewable on an OS-assigned ephemeral port hard-guarded â‰  8777.\n\nIn short: **Anchor is a local, plain-text, stdlib-Python productivity dashboard that has evolved into a \"mission control\" for running and tracking AI agent-trio R&D projects on the user's own machine.**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45325,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"421ffa6a-f444-4a42-81af-61b391ba9243","uuid":"4aa02c7f-6e45-4ebc-b370-1af5083cfd57","request_id":"req_011Cc1heF5yoCMgYypoNutce"}
